      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T10:49:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could be on the previous line, but more importantly I don\u0027t think this does what you want. This just gets the next callback and makes sure it\u0027s of type OnQosSessionAvailable, then it returns it, and on the returned value it executes a series of comparisons the result of which is thrown away. In other words, you\u0027ll fail this test if the callback is of the wrong type, but not if any of the tests below evaluate to false.\n\nI think you just wanted to remove () and .let, so that the block gets passed to expectCallback.\n\nThe same thing appplies in l.876.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 869,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 869,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "17d9f67dcf72944951b276a40e8791706f12a7f1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
