      "message": "Now that I could step back for a second, I see where the disconnect is.  There wasn\u0027t a version of expect callback that took in a function.  I added one on.\n\n(With that said, the let here is totally nonsensical.)\n\nI applied the same change everywhere.  But it, unfortunately, occurred to me, that using individual asserts probably make more sense in these cases.  Reason being is that if there is a failure, then we wouldn\u0027t know which of the comparison failed.  Let me know if you want me to switch back.\n\nFYI, this comment chain started here:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/1487838/11..19/tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NetworkAgentTest.kt#b892",
